    {
      "id": "claim_a953098db77041ba94c4c30348736f23",
      "statement": "The three EXIF libraries have disjoint roles: Pillow opens, decodes, rotates, and saves images and supplies ExifTags.TAGS for orientation lookup (UnidentifiedImageError signals undecodable files); exifread is read-only EXIF parsing used solely by get_date_taken; piexif is read/modify/write EXIF used solely by add_relative_path_tag. Each stage re-opens the file from disk; no in-memory image object is shared.",
      "evidence": [
